id: pm-github-hptv
title: Bound native Bun CLI repeats of a completed public atomic import
description: "The intermittent historical installed-Bun repeat has not reproduced in three fresh packed repeats and three live-public-snapshot repeats. A real dangling comment-lock symlink independently reproduced an unbounded busy loop, fixed by honoring the existing wait budget. Installed acceptance retains its 45-second execution deadline and now force-kills the process group after a separate five-second cleanup window; timeout always fails even on a later zero exit. Recent repeats preserve durable bytes and strict health. The historical root cause remains unestablished."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T08:28:54.625Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-06T11:44:34.944Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-sol
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T09:07:19.298Z",codex-sol,"A fresh bounded native Bun CLI repeat of the latest packed candidate passed in 4.22 seconds with exit zero and byte-identical tracker contents. This contrasts with the earlier long-running repeat, so retain the issue as an intermittent installed-host investigation rather than claiming a consistent Bun failure. All 375 native Bun library and operational tests also pass."
  "2026-10-05T09:55:33.050Z",codex-sol,"The final packed candidate matched all three authored runtime modules byte-for-byte. Its fresh Node public import passed with three issues, a byte-identical second run, zero gate findings, and strict health in 24.94 seconds. A bounded direct native Bun CLI repeat, using the same pinned host and startup executable path, timed out at 45.06 seconds and was terminated with SIGTERM; durable tracker bytes stayed unchanged. This reproduces the intermittent installed-host boundary alongside all 420 passing native Bun library and operational tests. No scratch remote was configured and no public-data push occurred."
  "2026-10-06T11:17:41.296Z",codex-sol,"Packed installed-CLI reproduction with the pinned host passes three consecutive native Bun repeats under the unchanged 45-second watchdog. The complete fixture test took 26.63 seconds, including packing, installation, Node import, and all three repeats; each retained item bytes and unchanged bare-remote refs. Separately reproduced a real dangling comment-lock symlink: open with exclusive creation returns EEXIST while stat returns ENOENT, causing the old immediate-continue path to busy-spin forever. The preserved fix adds sleep and checks the existing wait budget. This is a proven local lock defect, not yet proof of the historical installed-host timeout cause. Further public-data and diagnostic acceptance follows."
  "2026-10-06T11:33:55.510Z",codex-sol,"Fresh live public snapshot acceptance passed: one non-PR pm-todos issue updated since 2026-10-01, fetched with paginated gh reads, replayed unchanged through the packed candidate HTTP client and pinned host. Node import 2.49 seconds; byte-identical Node repeat 2.36 seconds; three byte-identical native Bun repeats 2.28, 2.03, and 2.33 seconds. Privacy PASS, strict health PASS, no remote configured. The complete all-state live import separately refused two email findings in older issue content before mutation, as required; no allowlist was added. Direct external HTTPS probes were intermittent, so the public snapshot receipt separates live retrieval from local installed-host execution. No deterministic SDK comment-add flakiness has reproduced; real create/comment/deduplication and permission-failure tests pass."
  "2026-10-06T11:37:10.437Z",codex-sol,"Acceptance now uses a shared process-group watchdog: the original 45-second deadline sends SIGTERM, then a separate five-second cleanup window sends SIGKILL. A timed-out command is always rejected, even if it exits zero afterward, and no writer step follows. The deterministic negative control uses a real CPU-spinning child that ignores SIGTERM; the watchdog force-kills it with unchanged durable fixture bytes. This bounds the historical installed-host timeout without claiming the dangling-lock defect was its original cause or increasing the execution deadline. The CLI lock defect itself now honors its existing wait budget."
  "2026-10-06T11:44:34.944Z",codex-sol,"Final frozen packed acceptance passes: one live public snapshot issue imported with gate PASS; Node import 4.02 seconds and byte-identical Node repeat 4.33 seconds; three native Bun repeats 3.36, 3.47 and 4.18 seconds with gate PASS and unchanged durable tracker bytes. Strict health passes in the disposable pinned-host project, with no remote configured. The spinning-child watchdog negative control also passes natively under Bun. Historical timeout cause remains unestablished; no deterministic SDK comment-add flakiness reproduced."
